comment_data.body:
I'm also unsure about shortening anything besides `$HOME`. I understand that Justin did say:

> - extra readable "compression": a dictionary substitution of known prefixes (`$HOME`, cwd, `stdpath('data')`, plugin roots).

@justinmk would love your feedback on whether you still feel `stdpath()` needs to be explicitly shortened at all. While the slug would be longer, I feel like the consistency of having fewer prefix exceptions can make the slug clearer. Plus, at least for the undofile and swapfile uses, it's not typical to open files in `stdpath('data')`, `stdpath('state')`, and `stdpath('cache')` in Nvim.
